# Isolated eval package — nested ignore so its own artifacts can never be
# committed, without touching the root .gitignore (which only anchors
# `/node_modules` at the repo root, not nested ones — see this package's
# own README for why this file exists as a separate, narrowly-scoped
# mechanism rather than a broader root-level change).

# Dependencies (own lockfile is committed; the installed tree is not).
node_modules/

# Local secrets — this package is never allowed to read a committed .env
# file (see README's own "Secret handling" section); this entry exists as
# defense-in-depth only, since no code path here ever writes one.
.env
.env.*

# Live benchmark outputs, human-scoring packets, and raw vendor
# diagnostics — synthetic-fixture-derived but still local-only by design
# (see README's own "Report artifacts" section). Fixtures and case
# definitions themselves are NOT covered by this pattern — they live
# under fixtures/ and cases.ts, both committed intentionally.
/results/
